{
  "about": "MobaLedLib hardware modules for a chain view. Not from the Excel workbook: a deliberate exception, the facts come from wiki.mobaledlib.de (source per module). Nothing here changes LEDs_AutoProg.h. 'unconfirmed' lists what no source confirms yet. Ports are the data-port ids in the SVG. 'leds' is how many LED numbers the module takes in the chain, 'channels' how many single outputs (3 per WS2811). A signal's 'drives' says, per workbook signal macro, which output lights each lamp: Cn is the n-th single output from the macro's LED (WS2811), Ln the n-th WS2812 after it; found by running each macro in the simulator (issue #19).",
  "categories": {
    "led": { "name": "LED module", "color": "#F5C76A" },
    "splitter": { "name": "Splitter", "color": "#5BD48A" },
    "controller": { "name": "Controller", "color": "#5BD48A" },
    "light": { "name": "Light", "color": "#F5C76A" },
    "signal": { "name": "Signal", "color": "#FF7A6B" }
  },
  "connectors": {
    "wanne6": {
      "name": "6-pin box header (Wannenstecker)",
      "pins": { "1": "+5V", "2": "data out (to the LEDs)", "3": "GND", "4": "data return (back to the splitter)", "5": "GND", "6": "+12V (optional)" },
      "source": "https://wiki.mobaledlib.de/anleitungen/bauanleitungen/verteilerplatine_200de"
    }
  },
  "modules": [
    {
      "id": "mll101",
      "name": "LichtMaschine Classic (101)",
      "svg": "mll101.svg",
      "category": "controller",
      "ports": [
        { "id": "led0", "kind": "led-channel", "channel": 0, "direction": "out" },
        { "id": "led2", "kind": "led-channel", "channel": 2, "direction": "out" },
        { "id": "hb_led0", "kind": "heartbeat-led" },
        { "id": "hb_led2", "kind": "heartbeat-led" },
        { "id": "can", "kind": "bus" },
        { "id": "key80", "kind": "inputs" },
        { "id": "keyboard", "kind": "inputs" }
      ],
      "facts": [
        "2 LED channels, numbered 0 and 2, each fused at 1 A",
        "each channel has a heartbeat LED at its output and one at its input",
        "768 single LEDs or 256 RGB LEDs; DCC, CAN, LNet, Selectrix"
      ],
      "unconfirmed": [
        "pin count of each connector (the wiki lists 3x 6-pin, 2x 8-pin, 1x 14-pin)",
        "whether the heartbeat LEDs take LED numbers in the chain",
        "DCC and power terminals are not drawn"
      ],
      "source": [
        "https://wiki.mobaledlib.de/anleitungen/bauanleitungen/101_v2/start",
        "https://wiki.mobaledlib.de/anleitungen/ueberblick_platinen"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "mll201",
      "name": "Universal Verteiler Pro (201)",
      "svg": "mll201.svg",
      "category": "splitter",
      "leds": 2,
      "ports": [
        { "id": "in", "kind": "wanne6", "direction": "in" },
        { "id": "out1", "kind": "wanne6", "direction": "out-return" },
        { "id": "out2", "kind": "wanne6", "direction": "out-return" },
        { "id": "out3", "kind": "wanne6", "direction": "out-return" },
        { "id": "out4", "kind": "wanne6", "direction": "out-return" },
        { "id": "out5", "kind": "wanne6", "direction": "out-return" },
        { "id": "out6", "kind": "wanne6", "direction": "out-return" },
        { "id": "out7", "kind": "wanne6", "direction": "out-return" },
        { "id": "out8", "kind": "wanne6", "direction": "out-return" },
        { "id": "out9", "kind": "wanne6", "direction": "out-return" },
        { "id": "out10", "kind": "wanne6", "direction": "out-return" },
        { "id": "out11", "kind": "wanne6", "direction": "out-return" },
        { "id": "out12", "kind": "wanne6", "direction": "out-return" },
        { "id": "next", "kind": "wanne6", "direction": "out-return" },
        { "id": "led_fwd", "kind": "amplifier-led" },
        { "id": "led_back", "kind": "amplifier-led" }
      ],
      "facts": [
        "12 outputs plus 'Next' to the next splitter; 'Next' is the last channel and has no DIP switch",
        "a 12-way DIP switch bridges each unused output",
        "two WS2812 amplify the signal: FWD at the input, BACK in the return path",
        "the input LED is defined first, the return LED at the end of the chain or of each branch",
        "separate 5V and 12V terminals, at most 2.5 A per voltage; flat cables are rated at 1 A",
        "between splitters, chain only 4-pole cables (data only, no power)"
      ],
      "unconfirmed": [
        "the connector pinout is taken from the 200 page; the 201 page says its connectors follow the 200",
        "the 5V/12V power terminals are not drawn"
      ],
      "source": [
        "https://wiki.mobaledlib.de/anleitungen/bauanleitungen/verteilerplatine_201de",
        "https://wiki.mobaledlib.de/anleitungen/bauanleitungen/verteilerplatine_200de"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "mll503",
      "name": "WS2811 Multi-Use v2 (503)",
      "svg": "mll503.svg",
      "category": "led",
      "leds": 12,
      "channels": 36,
      "sections": [
        { "section": 1, "leds": 4, "return": "t1" },
        { "section": 2, "leds": 4, "return": "t2" },
        { "section": 3, "leds": 4, "return": "t3" }
      ],
      "ports": [
        { "id": "in", "kind": "wanne6", "direction": "in" },
        { "id": "t1", "kind": "return-jumper" },
        { "id": "t2", "kind": "return-jumper" },
        { "id": "t3", "kind": "return-jumper" },
        { "id": "dout", "kind": "data", "direction": "out" }
      ],
      "facts": [
        "12 WS2811F chips (v1 had 10), 3 outputs each: up to 36 single LEDs; can also feed series circuits on 12 V",
        "three sections that can be cut apart",
        "when nothing follows, solder jumpers T1/T2/T3 loop the signal back to the input: T2 if section 3 is cut off, T1 if sections 2 and 3 are cut off"
      ],
      "unconfirmed": [
        "4 chips per section (12 chips in 3 equal sections)",
        "positions of the pads and of T1-T3"
      ],
      "source": ["https://wiki.mobaledlib.de/anleitungen/bauanleitungen/503de_multi-use_v2"]
    },
    {
      "id": "mll504",
      "name": "WS2811 Multi-Use Micro (504)",
      "svg": "mll504.svg",
      "category": "led",
      "leds": 2,
      "channels": 6,
      "ports": [
        { "id": "in", "kind": "data", "direction": "in" },
        { "id": "out", "kind": "data", "direction": "out" },
        { "id": "5v_in", "kind": "power" },
        { "id": "gnd_in", "kind": "power" },
        { "id": "5v_out", "kind": "power" },
        { "id": "gnd_out", "kind": "power" }
      ],
      "facts": [
        "2 WS2811F chips: six single LEDs, three of them sharing each plus pole",
        "pad layout like a WS2812B (+5V, data in/out, GND), so it can replace a WS2812B in a chain",
        "up to about 1 A on its supply tracks"
      ],
      "unconfirmed": ["position of the pads"],
      "source": ["https://wiki.mobaledlib.de/anleitungen/bauanleitungen/504de_ws2811_multi-use-micro_v1"]
    },
    {
      "id": "mll521",
      "name": "24-Single LED Connector v2 (521)",
      "svg": "mll521.svg",
      "category": "led",
      "leds": 8,
      "channels": 24,
      "ports": [
        { "id": "in", "kind": "wanne6", "direction": "in" },
        { "id": "out", "kind": "wanne6", "direction": "out-return" }
      ],
      "facts": [
        "8 WS2811F chips: up to 24 single LEDs",
        "6-pin input and output; the 'Term' jumper in the output loops the signal back to the splitter",
        "separate 5V and 12V terminals; two-pole 12 V outputs for series circuits",
        "unused chips must be reserved with 'Reserve LEDs'",
        "24 x 18.5 mA = about 444 mA at full brightness"
      ],
      "unconfirmed": ["outputs 13-24 on the upper terminal row"],
      "source": ["https://wiki.mobaledlib.de/anleitungen/bauanleitungen/521de_single_connector_v2"]
    },
    {
      "id": "mll295",
      "name": "TinyHouse (295)",
      "svg": "mll295.svg",
      "category": "led",
      "channels": 6,
      "ports": [
        { "id": "in", "kind": "wanne6", "direction": "in" },
        { "id": "led1", "kind": "single-outputs", "channels": 3 },
        { "id": "led2", "kind": "single-outputs", "channels": 3 },
        { "id": "rgb3", "kind": "rgb-output", "direction": "out-return" },
        { "id": "rgb4", "kind": "rgb-output", "direction": "out-return" },
        { "id": "rgb5", "kind": "rgb-output", "direction": "out-return" },
        { "id": "heartbeat", "kind": "heartbeat-led" }
      ],
      "facts": [
        "six single LED outputs (LED1, LED2: R+, G+, B+), 5V or 12V per group of three by a solder jumper",
        "three RGB outputs (LED3-LED5: 5V, GND, data in/out), each with a solder jumper (NoLED, Skip4+5, ...); a jumper disables all following outputs, so fill them from right to left",
        "an onboard RGB heartbeat LED at the end of the data bus"
      ],
      "unconfirmed": [
        "number of LED numbers taken (depends on what is connected to LED3-LED5)",
        "the vertical pin row next to the input (5V DI GN DO GN 12V) is not drawn"
      ],
      "source": ["https://wiki.mobaledlib.de/anleitungen/bauanleitungen/295_tinyhouse"]
    },
